{"event":"answer","q":"How do I treat a snake bite?","lang":"en","alerts":[],"retrieved":[{"id":178,"source":"army-atp-4-02-11","score":0.0167,"cos":0.795},{"id":177,"source":"army-atp-4-02-11","score":0.0164,"cos":0.785},{"id":179,"source":"army-atp-4-02-11","score":0.0161,"cos":0.781},{"id":176,"source":"army-atp-4-02-11","score":0.0159,"cos":0.775}],"a":"Keep the bitten person still and calm while waiting for medical help [2, 3]. Clean the wound gently with mild soap and water and apply a sterile bandage over it [1]. Seek medical attention immediately after a snakebite is crucial to minimize venom effects [3, 4].","cited":[1,2,3,4],"invalid_citations":[],"grounded":true,"admits_gap":false,"no_source":false,"ttft_ms":326,"total_ms":805,"input_tokens":733,"output_tokens":57,"tokens_per_s":117.2,"rss_mb":4008}
